    "assistant_text": "Found it \u2014 the discount is being rounded per line item and accumulated, which loses a cent versus rounding once on the subtotal.\n\nMath check: per-line rounding gives discount = 9.32 + 35.22 + 61.12 = 105.66, so total_due = 1428.00 \u2212 105.66 + 2.50 = 1324.84 (test pays 1324.83 \u2192 UNDERPAID by 1 cent). Rounding the discount once on the subtotal instead gives 1428.00 \u00d7 0.074 = 105.672 \u2192 rounds to 105.67, so total_due = 1428.00 \u2212 105.67 + 2.50 = 1324.83 \u2014 exactly matching the test's payment.\nThe `ZERO` import in engine.py may now be unused \u2014 let me check and run the tests.\nAll 6 tests pass. `ZERO` is still used in `Invoice.subtotal()`, so no unused import.\n\n**Root cause:** `settle()` was rounding the promotional discount per line item and summing the rounded results, instead of rounding once on the invoice subtotal. That accumulated a 1-cent rounding error (105.66 vs. the correct 105.67), making `total_due` come out a cent too high and the exact-payment test read as `UNDERPAID`. Fixed in `src/ledger/engine.py` by computing `discount = rules.discount_for(subtotal)` directly.",
